What are Microfocus X-ray Sources?
Microfocus X-ray Sources are specialized X-ray generating devices characterized by an extremely small focal spot size—typically less than a few micrometers. This key feature minimizes geometric unsharpness, allowing for the capture of highly detailed, magnified images essential for sophisticated applications. These sources often employ standardized interfaces like RS-232C for external control and can produce exceptionally clear images even in complex 3D computed tomography (CT) scanning environments. They are integral to quality control, failure analysis, and research in fields requiring micron-level resolution.
